    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on high-upside speed threats against favorable pitching matchups. The anchor of our lineup is **Yordan Alvarez** (76.88), who benefits from a strong xwOBA of 0.450 and a neutral-to-favorable matchup against Bibee. However, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.81) represents our most surgical play; his combination of leadoff usage and a high-frequency SB opportunity against a slower delivery allows him to maximize our scarcest category. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (69.42) is in a prime spot against the 5.00 xERA of Poulin, providing the best power-hitting profile on the board despite the negative park factor.\n\nWe are navigating several high-leverage platoon situations to maintain efficiency. **Lars Nootbaar** (63.95) remains a strong start due to an 11% platoon bump against the right-handed Lugo, while **Dillon Dingler** (57.38) just misses the \"Strong\" threshold but holds significant value due to his position in the order and the wind favoring hitters. The tightest decision of the day fell on **Christian Yelich** (58.43), who edged out other bench options despite a tough left-on-left dynamic against P\u00e9rez. While **Christian Yelich** is technically on the bubble of our marginal range, his leadoff spot and elite floor keep him in the lineup over candidates like **Nelson Velazquez** or **Josh Smith**, who lack the same guaranteed plate appearances today. \n\nStrategic risk management remains critical as we monitor the lower end of the roster. **Colt Keith** (42.69) and **Casey Schmitt** (41.80) are hovering near our bench floor; while both carry the benefit of wind-aided offensive potential, their low scores reflect the difficulty of their respective matchups. We are consciously holding **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** on the bench today, though they are currently unavailable due to team off-days, alongside minor league stashes like **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds**. With no major weather concerns forecasted, the focus is squarely on maintaining our efficiency targets while balancing the limited game caps against the high-SB-potential plays of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin**.",
